<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Warad-Sin</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">r. c. 1834–1823 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century-bce">19th century BCE</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Warad-Sin was king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/larsa">Larsa</a> in southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mesopotamia">Mesopotamia</a>, installed by his father <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kudur-mabuk">Kudur-Mabuk</a>, an Amorite chief. During his reign he carried out extensive building works at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ur">Ur</a>, Larsa and other cities, and his father continued to exercise strong influence. He was succeeded by his brother <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rim-sin-i">Rim-Sin I</a>, who ruled Larsa for some sixty years.</p></div>
